https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w9qsDgA1q8Y  (Capo 5)

Mike Nesmith of The Monkees fame wrote this and his own version is quite nice in a totally different way with a country bent to it.  

TIP:  The (G) (Bm) (C) (D) progression moves right along.  Note the (Bm) comes in the last half of some syllables.  Just follow and feel the rhythm you won't have any problems.  Also, if playing untransposed you can simplify things by playing a 3-note (Bm) and it'll sound just fine and the transition is easier as the chord shape is very similar between the 3-note (Bm) and (C).

      
